{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483835-that-one-vtm-related-book-that-really-could-have-used-character-templates","id":1483835,"title":"That one VtM related book that really could have used character templates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-12T19:25:24-07:00","id":1483835,"title":"That one VtM related book that really could have used character templates","content":"I don't remember where I got it, but I have an old copy of Kindred of the East, and last night I went through it, looking for inspiration for a Chinese Vampire Prince. Now I didn't get much, other than the name for the restaurant she'll have built on top of her Court, but I noticed something weird. There are no Character Templates. <br /> <br /> If you've read at least partway into <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates\">this thread</a> by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\">No One of Consequence</a>, you'll notice White Wolf liked their character templates. They didn't just put them in their Clan books, they had templates for Ghouls, for Sabbat, for Caitiff. Even one of the books for the Black Hand had Character Templates. But I flipped through the whole Kindred of the East book and did not find a single one. I'm not trying to gripe (especially about a book published maybe a decade before Onyx Path started) but it seems strange.<br /> <br /> Surely if any sourcebook could have benefitted from some CTs it would have been the one with a previously unheard-of monster type, let alone one with five completely unfamiliar lineages such as the dharmas. Was there ever an explanation given for not including any?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T19:40:42-07:00","id":1483836,"title":"","content":"There were templates in the various Dharma books. Five each, IIRC. Kindred of the Ebony Kingdoms never got any expansion material though. Nor did Dark Ages' Veil of Night. So a lot of readers who aren't very familiar with those various cultures are usually left with only the most bare bones of cultural stereotypes they may have picked up from assorted Western-accessible media from the time. <br /> <br /> Of the first edition books, I think Hunters Hunted could've benefited from some pre-made character templates. The Year of the Hunter books had some, but I would've enjoyed a few totally independent ones to go with them. <br /> <br /> The Elysium/elders book also could've used a few so that we'd have examples of pre-made elder characters outside of the Black Hand cult. <br /> <br /> The Anarch Cookbook probably could've benefited from a couple as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T19:46:20-07:00","id":1483837,"title":"","content":"Didn't know KotE had Dharma books, but it still seems weird that the first book didn't have at least a few. I wonder if they ran too close to the deadline to add them. <br /> <br /> I doubt they were afraid of offending sensibilities. No offense intended to White Wolf, but they crossed that threshold so often they wore a ditch into it before KotE was even published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T20:19:56-07:00","id":1483839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483835-that-one-vtm-related-book-that-really-could-have-used-character-templates?p=1483837#post1483837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't know KotE had Dharma books, but it still seems weird that the first book didn't have at least a few. I wonder if they ran too close to the deadline to add them.<br /> <br /> I doubt they were afraid of offending sensibilities. No offense intended to White Wolf, but they crossed that threshold so often they wore a ditch into it before KotE was even published.</div> </div> </div> </div>More than likely they were cut for space.<br /> <br /> Premade characters while useful for inexperienced STs, are a waste of space for everyone else. Unlike the books for western inspired vampires and culture, the KotE books had to be a crash course on both asian history and culture in addition to explaining how it was altered to fit in the WoD setting.<br /> <br /> For context, the landmass of Texas is about the same size as the entire european theater for WWII. Inside that area you have the UK, France, Germany, Holland, Belgium, etc. That is a lot of different cultures, languages, social customs, and mythologies to draw from and explain. That same area only roughly covers China, which means you don't get to the other asian countries and cultures. They didn't even touch on India really until near the end of the game line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T20:44:42-07:00","id":1483842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1483835-that-one-vtm-related-book-that-really-could-have-used-character-templates?p=1483837#post1483837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't know KotE had Dharma books, but it still seems weird that the first book didn't have at least a few. I wonder if they ran too close to the deadline to add them.<br /> <br /> I doubt they were afraid of offending sensibilities. No offense intended to White Wolf, but they crossed that threshold so often they wore a ditch into it before KotE was even published.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Dharma books are fairly good, though I didn't care how the Cranes book was written mostly in-character. That said I think the Devil Tiger book is one of the best books that White Wolf ever published, so if you ever get the chance to check it out, I'd recommend doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T20:54:58-07:00","id":1483845,"title":"","content":"There was, once the popularity/sales of the original book warranted its expansion into a full line, a Companion, the five Dharma books, the single Heretical Dharmas book, the Dhampyrs book, the San Fransisco by Night book, The 1000 Hells, and one or two others, IIRC. There was also Sunset Empires, which was going to be a crossover with Victorian Age Vampire, but ended up only being a PDF release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T13:47:18-07:00","id":1483911,"title":"","content":"Corebooks did not tend to have templates. Templates were more of a Players Guide, splatbook, and faction book thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T16:12:43-07:00","id":1484055,"title":"","content":"IIRC, World of Darkness: Blood &amp; Silk, rather than templates, had a collection of character concepts and which Dharmas worked best with them. The idea ended up being repeated with Dark Ages: Vampire, with a bunch of concept ideas that each listed which Clans and Roads best fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}